<details class="corr-prof"><summary>Austro-Hungarian Empire <span class="corr-n">6</span></summary><p><a href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire">Read the profile of Austro-Hungarian Empire →</a></p><ul class="corr-list corr-short"><li><span class="corr-was">The dynasty's rule ended &quot;without even a final battle&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> the Italian victory at Vittorio Veneto and the armistice of Villa Giusti (3 November 1918) preceded the end.</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">Budapest &quot;grew from a modest town in 1867 to a metropolis of nearly one million by 1914&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> formed in 1873 from Buda, Óbuda and Pest; almost 900,000 by 1910 (Pest-Buda was already a substantial city in 1867); removed &quot;Europe's most extensive railway network east of Germany&quot; (Russia's was larger).</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">&quot;the sixth-largest GDP in the world by 1900&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;one of the larger industrial economies of continental Europe&quot; (unsupported ranking); &quot;Bohemia and Moravia ... approximately 60 percent of the empire's industrial output&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;the greater part of the Austrian half's industrial output&quot;.</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">Austrian half called &quot;the Austrian Empire (Cisleithania)&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> officially &quot;the Kingdoms and Lands represented in the Imperial Council&quot;.</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">Wilson's Fourteen Points &quot;demanded autonomy ... gave the succession movements international legal sanction&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> called for &quot;autonomous development&quot;; Allied recognition of the Czechoslovak Nati