<details class="corr-prof"><summary>Ghana Empire <span class="corr-n">8</span></summary><p><a href="/empire/ghana-empire">Read the profile of Ghana Empire →</a></p><ul class="corr-list corr-short"><li><span class="corr-was">Al-Bakri's &quot;guards wearing golden collars&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> guard dogs wearing collars of gold and silver (al-Bakri's account refers to the dogs)</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">Awdaghast &quot;previously held by Zanata Berbers&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> dominated by Sanhaja Berbers; &quot;northern terminus&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> southern end of the western trans-Saharan route</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">&quot;sub-kings, as al-Khwarizmi's world map of 833 CE noted&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> attributed to al-Yaqubi, late ninth century</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">Al-Fazari &quot;equal in size to the Idrisid state of Morocco&quot; (anachronistic: Idrisids founded 788, after the c. 777 date) <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> removed; &quot;Persian astronomer&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;the astronomer&quot;; date &quot;around 777 CE&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;late eighth century&quot;</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">Sosso &quot;began subjugating Wagadou around 1140&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> took over Wagadou in the early thirteenth century under Sumanguru Kante (date removed)</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">&quot;Sundiata Keita destroyed Koumbi Saleh in 1240&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> Sundiata defeated Sumanguru at Kirina c. 1235; capital traditionally abandoned c. 1240</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">&quot;Almoravid pressure forced conversion in 1076&quot; and &quot;sack of Koumbi Saleh around 1076&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> traditionally dated conquest; ruling house appears to have adopted Islam in the late eleventh century (contested)</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">&quot;only viable corridor&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;strategic zone&quot;; &quot;Carthaginian&quot; markets removed; Tichitt &quot;emerged from ... approximately 1600 BCE&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;often linked to ... second millennium BCE&quot;; iron vs &quot;stone or bone&quot; armed neighbours <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> softened; &quot;When Ghana gained independence&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;When the Gold Coast gained independence&quot;; impact &quot;Fatimid Caliphate ... Mediterranean Europe&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> North Africa and Muslim Spain</span></li></ul></details>
