<details class="corr-prof"><summary>Gupta Empire <span class="corr-n">6</span></summary><p><a href="/empire/gupta-empire">Read the profile of Gupta Empire →</a></p><ul class="corr-list corr-short"><li><span class="corr-was">Samudragupta &quot;defeated twelve northern kings outright&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> uprooted nine kings of the north; twelve southern rulers defeated and reinstated (Allahabad Pillar Inscription)</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">Aryabhata &quot;developed place-value notation&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> worked within the place-value decimal system (it predates him)</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">Sushruta presented as a Gupta-era physician <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> the Sushruta Samhita is an earlier compendium that continued to circulate and be revised; removed &quot;not matched in Western medicine for over a millennium&quot; (overstated)</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">Vishayapatis &quot;often drawn from local merchant guilds&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> appointed officials advised by councils including the chief banker, caravan merchant and head of artisans</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">&quot;chariot corps&quot; removed (chariots obsolete by this period); &quot;cavalry dominated tactical thinking&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> mounted archers increasingly prominent</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">Summary &quot;lasted barely two hundred years&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;two hundred and fifty years&quot; (c. 320 to c. 550); Hunas pressing &quot;around 458 CE&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;around the middle of the century&quot; (year removed); Faxian &quot;visiting between 399 