<details class="corr-prof"><summary>Mongol Empire <span class="corr-n">7</span></summary><p><a href="/empire/mongol-empire">Read the profile of Mongol Empire →</a></p><ul class="corr-list corr-short"><li><span class="corr-was">&quot;Following the death of Kublai Khan in 1294, central authority weakened, leading to fragmentation&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> fragmentation began after Möngke's death in 1259 with the Kublai–Ariq Böke war (1260–1264); 1294 retained as the end of the last widely recognised Great Khan.</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">&quot;The Yuan Dynasty in China fell to the Red Turban Rebellion in 1368&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> driven out by the Ming, founded by Zhu Yuanzhang, who rose in the Red Turban Rebellion.</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">&quot;fragmented Khwarazmian states&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> the newly expanded but poorly integrated Khwarazmian Empire (it was a large unified state in 1219).</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">&quot;Subutai extended campaigns into Eastern Europe and the Middle East&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> Subutai in the west (Kalka 1223, Legnica and Mohi 1241); the Middle Eastern campaign (Baghdad 1258) was Hülegü's.</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">regional khanates &quot;adhered to overarching Mongol political norms&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> largely independent after 1264, sharing Chinggisid heritage.</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">&quot;born Temüjin in 1162&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;around 1162&quot; (birth year disputed); Yassa &quot;codified law&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;traditionally attributed ... exact form uncertain&quot;.</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">&quot;Central Asian steppes&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;steppes of Mongolia&quot;.</span></li></ul></details>
