enue&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;a leading source&quot;; &quot;first European force to systematise pay&quot; softened; &quot;peasant representation that had no equivalent&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;few parallels among the major European states&quot;; &quot;three votes in the Imperial Diet&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;a voice in the Imperial Diet&quot; (cautious); &quot;Fabian strategy&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> scorched-earth retreat and attrition; &quot;population of barely 2.5 million&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> combined population of around 2.5 million.</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">Swedish rule over Finland &quot;(1249–1809)&quot; <span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only"> became </span> &quot;from the Middle Ages until 1809&quot; (1249 is a traditional date; year removed).</span></li><li><span class="corr-was">Poltava date marked as Old Style.</span></li></ul></details>
